{% set local_problem %}
<p>Lacey's Spring's hilly terrain makes downspout placement critical. Water follows the path of least resistance — if your downspouts are directing it toward your foundation instead of away, you're creating problems.</p>

<p>Many rural homes have downspout systems that weren't designed with the terrain in mind. Water may be dumped uphill of the foundation, in natural drainage channels that lead back to the house, or simply not far enough away.</p>

<p>We understand hillside drainage and design systems that work with your property's natural patterns.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>A good downspout system has three components: adequate capacity, proper positioning, and effective water dispersal. On hilly terrain, positioning is especially critical.</p>

<p>For many Lacey's Spring properties, underground drains work better than surface extensions because they can route water to the most effective discharge point regardless of surface grade.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We're based in Hartselle and understand rural Morgan County terrain. We'll design a system that works with your property — not against it.</p>
